Subject: [PATCH] T23: live (no-teardown) encoder reconfig + day/night keyframe
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (branch stable)
Stacks on: 0001 (daynight+JsonAPI Part-2), 0002 (VideoWorker teardown), 0003 (quiesce).
Applies cleanly with git apply -p1 / patch -p1 AFTER 0001-0003 (verified).

==== Why ====
On Ingenic T23 every encoder teardown/rebuild path is unreliable: an in-process
rebuild wedges the VPU after a few cycles (reboot-only), and 0001 Part-2 forces
exactly such a rebuild on every bitrate/fps/gop/qp change. The reliable way to
change those runtime knobs is to reconfigure the RUNNING encoder live, with no
teardown, using the T23 libimp setters confirmed present on this camera and
verified against include/T23/1.3.0/zh/imp/imp_encoder.h:
  bitrate/QP  -> IMP_Encoder_Get/SetChnAttrRcMode (+ RequestIDR)
  fps         -> IMP_Encoder_SetChnFrmRate
  gop         -> IMP_Encoder_SetGOPSize

==== What ====
1) IMPEncoder gains T23-only setLiveBitrate/setLiveFps/setLiveGop/setLiveQp.
   Get->modify-only-the-active-rcMode-field->Set->RequestIDR. No teardown.
2) video_stream gains req_bitrate/fps/gop/qp_min/qp_max + reconfig atomics
   (mirrors the existing jpeg_stream req_*/reconfig idiom).
3) JsonAPI handle_stream: on T23 the live fields (bitrate/fps/gop/qp_min/qp_max)
   are marked live=true so add_int does NOT set global_restart_video (i.e. it
   no longer rebuilds for them — supersedes 0001 Part-2 for these fields), and
   their new values are queued on global_video[idx]. "mode" no longer rebuilds
   on T23 (the SoC forces CBR, so it is cosmetic). Structural fields
   (enabled/width/height/format/profile/buffers) keep 0001's rebuild path —
   they have no live setter on T23.
4) VideoWorker applies the queued reconfig at the top of its run loop — on the
   SAME thread that owns IMP_Encoder_GetStream, so the SDK setters are never
   concurrent with GetStream and need no lock; never tears anything down.
5) DayNightWorker::apply_mode sets idr_fix=1 on both video channels after the
   colour<->mono switch, so the worker emits a keyframe and the day/night
   transition no longer shows colour/mono corruption (issue 3).

Everything new is guarded by PLATFORM_T23; non-T23 builds are byte-identical to
the 0001-0003 stack.

diff --git a/src/DayNightWorker.cpp b/src/DayNightWorker.cpp
index 87b89fc..3ef7634 100644
--- a/src/DayNightWorker.cpp
+++ b/src/DayNightWorker.cpp
@@ -345,6 +345,19 @@ static void apply_mode(DayNightAlgo::Mode m) {
     std::string cmd = std::string(script) + " night";
     (void)std::system(cmd.c_str());
   }
+
+  // Force a clean keyframe on the active video channels right after the
+  // colour<->mono cut. Without it the decoder keeps predicting from pre-switch
+  // reference frames across the colourspace change, which shows as colour/mono
+  // corruption until the next scheduled IDR. Use the existing idr_fix flag so
+  // the VideoWorker thread (not this DayNightWorker thread) issues
+  // IMP_Encoder_RequestIDR — matching prudynt's own cross-thread IDR idiom
+  // (JsonAPI request_idr -> idr_fix -> VideoWorker).
+  for (int i = 0; i < NUM_VIDEO_CHANNELS; ++i) {
+    if (global_video[i]) {
+      global_video[i]->idr_fix = 1;
+    }
+  }
 }
 
